libreac (1.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * reac.h: the 1.8.0 entry names the ABI the define holds, 6 (#23)
  * libreac 1.8.0
  * fuzz/README: the records, the ratchet, the contract lines and the 0-byte
    pcap rule (#23)
  * fuzz: raise the pcap floor to 80 covered lines (#23)
  * headers: the braid map is held to its harness copy; a 0-byte pcap buffer
    skips nothing (#23)
  * fuzz/sabotage: each patch names its check and its seed, and fuzz-records
    proves both (#23)
  * fuzz, headers: the scene trailer stays the library's own; citations name
    today's lines (#23)
  * fuzz_grant: group B polls the header's six addresses; group A's DT1 sum
    in the harness (#23)
  * fuzz_decode: check every sample against the braid map, and count the
    width itself (#23)
  * fuzz, headers: every rule a harness copied names its contract (#23)
  * pcap_source: skip a record of 0 bytes; 0 means the end of the file only
    (#23)
  * headers: a refused decode or scene build leaves its output untouched (#23)
  * fuzz: prove every mutant record at this commit, and refuse a check
    without one (#23)
  * fuzz: generate the seeds the new records name (#23)
  * fuzz: take the per-check harness rewrite from Theorem Labs (#23)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:20:36 +0000
